{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for exact abc7dcd03bc476889c1e9a40f3dd7f90b62bb06a, sole primary 7101db90 (notes/2026-10-15-hosted-counter-contracts.md). Design review only.\n\nF1 P2 — make the declared utterance rule enforce the promised numeral boundary (sections 3 and 7.3). A direct probe of the pinned evaluator returned true for n=3 with utterance \"13\" and \"x3x\", as well as \"3\" and \"number 3\". Concatenation \u0026 works, but $contains is substring matching. The host whole-token filter does not protect generic native say submissions. Define the intended boundary exactly and enforce it in the declared definition using supported bounded expressions, or choose a simpler native representation whose checked field actually guarantees the intended output. Witness native say admissions/refusals for exact numeral, embedded digits, embedded letters, punctuation and Unicode; use the same semantics at the host boundary.\n\nF2 P2 — retain a durable way to observe resume (sections 7.2 and 7.4). When every role is paused the alarm is disabled. The only remaining observer is a finite read session/stream; a restart closes that stream. A later resume-role is an ordinary team-scope act, and agent-team declares no sends, so that act need not invoke AgentTeam. After stream loss there is no specified event that recreates the observer. Keep bounded control catch-up while attached and paused, or define an equally durable authorized wake protocol for every relevant control. Cover pause-all, stream expiry/object eviction, then resume through generic MCP with no browser or host-status request; eligible work must resume. Also cover initially zero live rows followed by first setup/control.\n\nF3 P2 — replace the asserted universal input-cost bound with a model admission contract (section 6). inputBytes+256 is not yet justified for the selected models' actual chat framing/tokenization; a messages/usage smoke test does not prove an upper bound. Missing usage and restart charging depend on this being an upper bound. Require each catalog entry to retain a defensible bound for the complete provider input, including framing/special tokens and any charged token categories, plus an enforced output bound; unsupported models remain unavailable. Define settlement for malformed usage or reported cost above the reservation (preserve charges, fence subsequent calls, no silent clamp/release). A finite model-specific maximum can be simpler than a tokenizer claim. Witness limits, absent/invalid usage, and above-bound reports. The new four-model catalog and 5,000-Neuron default do not supply that admission proof. Cloudflare publishes model-specific token/Neuron rates: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers-ai/platform/pricing/ ; its binding contract: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers-ai/configuration/bindings/ . Neither establishes this note's fixed 256 framing allowance.\n\nArchitecture — the separate declared team scope plus one exact host attachment is a reasonable settings owner; settings need not move into Counter. Preserve full Counter/team ScopeRefs including incarnation and verify declared-definition/factory affiliation at attachment, rather than trusting the app field alone. One custody/ledger/assignment object is the useful simplification. F2 is the missing recovery edge.\n\nSecurity — retaining model output as data, no bearer/signing route/tools, separate administer/configure grants and controller checks are sound boundaries. The intended native output invariant and reservation bound still require F1/F3. Status read access by live agents.configure or agents.administer is consistent with the stated admin-only initial configuration policy; it need not be public. The new control domain must retain the existing signed-envelope operation/subject/body/deadline binding, not merely a standing check.\n\nSimplification — keep one native utterance validation rule and one host owner. Keep model-specific admissibility and cost assumptions in the catalog. Do not add a harness, sandbox or another identity mechanism to solve these findings.\n\nAnswers to explicit checker questions: \u0026 produces the numeral string, but $contains fails the whole-token requirement (F1). A focused applicationValues probe with declared scope field accepted and preserved a full lane ScopeRef and injected the trusted opener; this proves typed genesis transport, not scope creation or authority affiliation. The new definitions still need their proposed in-memory judgments. The universal byte/framing bound is unproven (F3). Status-role answer is above.\n\nNonblocking contract clarifications for the next draft: (a) The parent explicitly permits an administrative ceiling reduction below spent/reserved usage as a prospective fence. State whether set-allocation may similarly lower a role below its historical charges, and show used/reserved/remaining without erasing charges or implying that history was freed. Test generic scope control plus concurrent reservation. (b) Reservation precedes commit while its ID names a promise: specify a stable provisional identity and binding to the admitted promise, including the already owed commit/assignment crash witness. (c) Treat abort/timeout as local cancellation unless provider completion is proved; retain unresolved cost and distinguish one active local dispatch from possible still-running provider work after a timeout/restart. The reviewed documentation does not establish physical provider cancellation by env.AI.run(...,{signal}).\n\nValidation: exact note, parent sections and the full 86f8→abc7 delta read; relevant native definition/evaluator/factory/session/custody boundaries inspected; pure evaluator and typed-genesis probes run. No source edits, gate rerun, live provider call, GitHub push or Cloudflare deployment. The successor records written output, builder UI ownership after M1 install, catalog/defaults, and one paid retry after lost output. Those decisions are incorporated in this review; the deployment hold remains. The paid retry is reasonable for data-only output with a separately retained charged reservation.\n\nCatalog delta: all four quoted Neuron rate pairs match the current official pricing page (read 15 October). The GLM model schema exposes max_completion_tokens (max_tokens deprecated), whereas Qwen exposes max_tokens and applies a chat template unless raw is true; catalog adapters must state their exact parameter/usage mapping, rather than assume one generic maxOutput wire field. Sources: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers-ai/models/glm-4.7-flash/ and https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers-ai/models/qwen3-30b-a3b-fp8/ . The arithmetic for the asserted default bound is internally correct; its premise remains F3. Retrying after a timeout/restart also makes the physical/local concurrency distinction particularly relevant. Prior observations0f5a0ae0 were retained on retired86f8, not filed as its review verdict.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7101db902e5c7b81fc6372484a009f62164e697c","binding":"assigned","head":"abc7dcd03bc476889c1e9a40f3dd7f90b62bb06a","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:532905489d254612c99ae665989a13538083364f\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:30ea3552319353ce5b85ff41a824d87eb7656478\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:532905489d254612c99ae665989a13538083364f","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}